\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::2>
\f1\fs22 The Cloudborne came away glad in their hearts that The Dawkins would deliver them from the religion of Latter Day Capitalism (
\f2\i Praise him!
\f1\i0 ); the Elvi heard that The Dawkins would deliver science and reason to vanquish The Holy Rollers (
\f2\i Praise him!
\f1\i0 ); and the Airborne kids, who had never been so toxically drunk or so ecstatically down in the mud in their lives, just wanted to stick it up their parents\'92 tax-deductible bribery trusts.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 It was a warm, balmy night in November, the kind of night in which activism has been para-scientifically proven to foment. A crowd of a few thousand loitered while the crew packed away gear and started to pull down the stage. Elvi went amongst them with guitars\'97many who had not performed on stage\'97and entertained small audiences unwilling to let the night end. Out of respect for the High Elvis, they all adhered to his first little law, and sang the words of the Great Teacher, thereby rendering the other two surplus to the occasion. Or rather, they 
\f2\i mostly 
\f1\i0 sang the Great Teacher\'92s lyrics, having decided the Sages\'92 little ditty was unacceptable too, as it had been allowed by the High Elvis.\
Around four in the morning\'97which in Elvi time is regarded as still last night\'97security began chasing the stragglers off The Domain. Young Airborne, unused to being chased off anything, began rounding everyone up with a plan to relocate the party, herding hundreds of concert goers to hover-pad stalks where they exploited their credentials in elevators to ferry every Elvis and Cloudborne up to the centre of the business and political district, above the Layer, into a clear night of stars, moonlight, gleaming towers, street lights that actually worked, and something that hit the back of their throats like ice, but just turned out to be fresh harbour air.\
From the beginning, the Airborne exercised their allowance accounts, and ordered the night to be comfortable. They settled into Bent Street Plaza (named after the old Bent Street on the ground, which itself was both bent and named after a judge) at the base of TRAMPS Tower, and immediately ordered blankets and pillows delivered by bewildered and sometimes threatened events planners. Someone ordered catering-grade umbrella/patio heaters. More goods and furnishings arrived as they sang through the wee hours, led by the Elvi. Couches arrived and got passed overhead like crowd-surfing hippopotamuses until someone decided they\'92d rather sit in them right there, thank you very much. A pop-up bar popped up. A coffee cart was carted in. So was a pair of go-karts, and anyone who wanted to race them had to take them down to the Spring Street end of the plaza.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::2><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 The sun came up over the Layer exactly the way it doesn\'92t underneath it, and greeted almost no one other than our protesters awake enough to appreciate it. On a Sunday, the central business and political district was a ghost town, but it\'92s doubtful anyone would have sent the riot squad in when your shareholders\'92 children formed nearly half the protest.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::2>
\f1\fs22 As dawn broke, somebody ordered a marquee. Someone else, gloriously, hired a yurt. The coffee cart was overwhelmed by go-kart racers, so the Elvi called The Ghetto for coffee urns. Everyone drank coffee\'97they were going to need it. The Elvi sent for barbecue trailers too, each with enough grilling area to cook a water buffalo and three small crocodiles. Airborne kids tried to buy three small crocodiles\'97and it was unclear whether they intended to cook them or race the go-karts around them\'97but the soonest they could arrive was three weeks from Wednesday. As exotic as barbecued crocodile sounded to the Cloudborne, the Airborne boggled when the Elvi offered them an alternative grocery list.\
\'93This will be better than drugs,\'94 one of them said, and started placing the orders.\
An Elvis grabbed the list and scrawled 
\f2\i amphetamines 
\f1\i0 across the bottom.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::2><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 The Airborne kids were determined to eat everything offered them like tourists at a food orgy. The bacon was properly burned black, the eggs hard-scrambled and the pork sausage patties shallow-fried on the hotplates in the tide of residual bacon fat. Peanut butter and banana sandwiches were flattened on the plates and singed crisp. For anyone brave enough, there was fool\'92s gold loaf. Though the Cloudborne were wary, the Airborne ate the stuff until they started hallucinating on the sugar content.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::2>
\f1\fs22 Only the Elvi ate the buttermilk biscuits in sawmill gravy.\
Everyone drank more coffee. They were still going to need it.\
The crowd swelled and more provisions were ordered; breakfast lasted three hours, by which time the crowd had swelled to many thousands.\
Walter was elected Mayor of the Yurt. His first act in office was to convert it into a frozen yoghurt outlet, on the grounds that every festival needs an ice-cream parlour. He called it the Frogurt Yurt.\
The Elvi called for more instruments and the means to amplify them. They ordered tatami mats and taught karate while they set up an improvised stage. \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 Airborne kids sat cross-legged on mats and couches with borrowed guitars while Elvi taught them the same four chords with the patience they otherwise reserved for pet chimpanzees and drummers.\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\
Someone realised they\'92d better get portaloos. Pissing off the plaza into the Layer seemed less glamorous in full daylight; and in the middle of the night, a Cloudborne had almost fallen in while hanging their butt over the railing.\
After breakfast, a lad painted 
\fs20 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 OCCUPY BENT STREET
\fs22  across a tarpaulin in dripping black, and stood back from it, pleased. A girl beside him read it twice and shook her head, and painted her own slogan on another tarp: 
\fs20 GET BENT
\fs22 . The two slogans quickly appeared on Instagroan accounts, with invitations to show up and protest against Latter Day Capitalism, Airbornism, and the appalling state of the crocodile home delivery market. Someone tried to crack a joke about the crocodiles arriving in thirty minutes or they\'92re free, but no one quite laughed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::2>
\f1\fs22 An Elvine, who claimed to be in American Sound Studio the day the Great Teacher had discovered the words of The Dawkins, attracted a continually refreshing semicircle of folks from all classes as she told and explained the Words of The Dawkins. She told them about evolution, the one long blind accident, the survival of the fittest, the Holy Momma who The Dawkins foretold and who bore the Elvi in a shotgun house with the power off. The audience listened, chins on knees, to a doctrine of natural selection recited to dozens of folks each time, many of whom had never once been selected against, and found it, they said, incredibly deep. With each telling, someone would always ask:\
\'93Are we really descended from monkeys?\'94\
To which the Elvine answered, \'93You are, but what am I?\'94\
In the smarter groups, the answer came back, \'93A monkey,\'94 and everyone had a really good laugh.\
Eventually, more Elvi joined the groups and testified about what The Dawkins taught and what it meant to them, which was some variation of:\
\'93Even though I\'92m a descendant of a clone, no one has the right to think they are better or even different from me.\'94\
The Elvi received that as affirmation, the Cloudborne with the curiosity of possibilities. The Airborne mostly sighed with relief. As one Airborne said, \'93We never believed that, which just made it all the more important to act like we did. None of us ever wanted to be accused of being Cloudborne underneath it all.\'94\
The frogurt turned out to be the best way Walter had ever met girls\'97he almost forgot Kathy\'97and he loved to watch them eat the stuff.\
By eleven, the music had found its second wind\'97or more precisely, its second source of power\'97when the Elvi jacked in to a basement substation. The Elvi formed bands, and any Airborne kid was allowed to join, although they were given fairly simple guitar parts for only a song or two. A running sheet and set lists were drawn up and an improvised second day of music festivities gained momentum in a city district mostly vacated by office workers and residents\'85 The residents, truth be known, were probably spending the day in Tahiti, or at degustation banquets in the desert, or at tree-felling ceremonies in rainforests that were being taught to stand on their own two stumps and carry their own damn economic weight.\
As the morning progressed to afternoon, the bands improved, the transitions between sets went smoother and the crowd sang ever-louder as the drum kit was reconfigured and a fresh tray of guitars was placed on stage:\
