\f1\fs22 The chanting continued for over a minute while every Elvis within bowed their head and clasped their hands at the belt buckle. The crowd pressed at Chanta, and he was unsure how or why he was travelling through them as if gravity had laid down for a nap and accidentally propelling him through a crowd that parted as before the bow of a ship or an especially impressive golf cart. Reverent hands guided his elbows, and he found himself walking up stairs, on to a stage, to the front where the frontman welcomed him and showed him his thousands of fans.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<$Scr_Ps::2>
\f1\fs22 The crowd cheered as loud, Chanta thought, as the singing of thousands of Double Drummers, thousands more Greengrocers, and thousands more Black Princes too, with swarms of Floury Bakers and Cherrynoses thrown in. He stood paralysed. The front man tapped him on the elbow and offered him the mic. He took the mic and, unsure what to do with it, looked down at it while the sound of hundreds of thousands of cicadas sang their summer mating calls.\
A hundred eternities passed until the crowd quietened a little.\
\'93Hello\'85 I\'92m, um\'85 I\'92m Chanta\'85\'94\
The crowd went clich\'e9-grade crazy. Chanta lost both the ability and his will to speak.\
\'93Can I get you something?\'94 the band frontman asked him.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \'93I could really go a beer,\'94 Chanta croaked into the mic.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The crowd went Papal-Mass-level-wild.\
\'93Just tell them a little about yourself, like you would someone you meet at a bar,\'94 the frontman encouraged.\
\'93Would you like to come back to my place and see my floor polishers?\'94 He asked the frontman while still talking into the mic.\
The crowd agreed they would, at a volume that would have terrified Spinal Tap.\
Chanta recovered some of his wits, which were sadly insufficient for saying anything coherent.\
\'93I mean\'85 I run Enchanted Cleaning Services. No job too small, or murder scene too messy.\'94\
Six Elvi arrived with six eskies, set them down and threw their lids off; they were full of beers and ice. Chanta grabbed a beer and guzzled. At the back of stage, the band was already making a song with what they had:\
