\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::2>
\f1\fs22 On surveying the crowd, the stage, the furnishings, the jumping castle that had been turned into a mud-wrestling ring, the barbecues, the High Elvis declared the remainder of the planned festival activities would be relocated here. He ordered more portaloos.\
Then he chartered two buses and offered Ghetto tours to the Airborne kids.\
Two buses were not enough. The High Elvis happily organised more. Though tourism and public relations were considerations, he planned on keeping hostages in the Ghetto if the situation required, assessing the kids would treat it as an adventure.\
The show runner consulted his clipboard and \'91found\'92 a slot for the High Elvis to perform mid-afternoon. The High Elvis wanted to play at night with a full light show but advisers dissuaded him from taking a full concert production past sundown on a Sunday.\
The High Elvis\'92s set ran the same as his performance the night before, without the interruption of the Sages, and with more breaks to speak to the crowd. He spoke of The Dawkins and his ideas of evolution. The crowd especially liked the part about the Airborne and Cloudborne evolving from monkeys. Suddenly, Latter Day Capitalists seemed less virtuous, the Cloudborne less hopeless, and the Elvi the best thing for music since Beethoven invented the blues.\
By the time the High Elvis had finished his set, t-shirts were being handed out free, the cost met by an Airborne start-up that had started up on the plaza to give away t-shirts. There was only one design, depicting a chimpanzee playing air guitar with the caption 
\fs20 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 GET BENT.
